ig02-rolling-update-maxsurge-maxunavailable\"\n178\t  - \"ch06-fig03-recreate-vs-rolling\"\n179\t  - \"ch06-fig04-workload-resource-decision-tree\"\n180\t  - \"ch06-fig05-statefulset-vs-deployment-identity\"\n181\t  - \"ch06-zenith-control-loop-instantiated\"\n182\t---\n183\t\n184\t# Chapter 6 Outline — Fleets, Not Vessels\n185\t\n186\t## Chapter-type note (read first)\n187\t\n188\t`chapter_type: content`. No contract exemptions apply. Drafting must deliver every required element:\n189\t\n190\t| Required element | Strictness | Where it lands |\n191\t|---|---|---|\n192\t| `# Chapter 6: Fleets, Not Vessels` | required | top |\n193\t| `## *\"Nobody sails one Pod\"*` | required | line 2 |\n194\t| Metadata line (weight / complexity / novelty) | required | after subtitle |\n195\t| `## Attention Budget` | required | before epigraph |\n196\t| Epigraph blockquote | expected | after Attention Budget |\n197\t| `## 🧭 Soundings` | expected | after epigraph — **8 questions** (content baseline) |\n198\t| `## Why This Chapter Matters` | **required** | after Soundings |\n199\t| `## What You'll Learn` | expected | after Why-This-Chapter-Matters |\n200\t| `## ☆ Taking Your Bearings #1–#3` | **required, min 2** | after §3, §5, §8 |\n201\t| `★ Fixed Point` ×6 | **required, min 1** | §1, §3, §4, §5, §6, §7 |\n202\t| `**Dead Reckoning:**` ×1 min | **required** | §4 — rolling-update mechanics stated flat, no fleet register |\n203\t| `⚠ Navigational Hazards` ×2 | expected, min 1 | §5 (the revision rule), §7 (the three sibling-resource traps, one root cause) |\n204\t| `☀️ Zenith` | expected | §9 |\n205\t| `## Exam Alert` | **required** | after §9 |\n206\t| `## Practice Questions` | **required** | 19 questions |\n207\t| `## Chapter Summary` | **required** | table |\n208\t| `## The Voyage Ahead` | **required** | closing — name locked 2026-04-19 |\n209\t| `🏆 Safe Harbor` | expected | chapter close |\n210\t\n211\tHeading form follows the shipped chapters exactly: `## ⚪ §1 — The Resource That Holds the Intent`, and checkpoints as `## ☆ Taking Your Bearings #1`.\n212\t\n213\t**Zenith:** exactly one, per Part 18.10. `ch06-zenith-control-loop-instantiated` in §9. This chapter carries five concept diagrams plus the Zenith — the same load as Chapters 4 and 5, at the upper end of the 2–8 band. `ch06-fig04` (the decision tree) will be the tempting one to inflate into a second Zenith because it is the figure readers will photograph. Resist. Its job is reference; §9's job is recognition.\n214\t\n215\t**Attention Budget guidance for drafting.** Nine sections, five distinct costs:\n216\t\n217\t| Section | Cost | Why |\n218\t|---|---|---|\n219\t| §1 | medium | One reframe (you will almost never create a Pod) plus a three-layer ownership chain that has to survive six later chapters |\n220\t| §2 | low | The reader already owns the control loop from Ch 3. This section makes it concrete and adds one field |\n221\t| §3 | medium | The selector mechanism, plus a consequence (template labels must agree) that is not obvious |\n222\t| §4 | **high** | Two strategies, two tunable bounds with defaults, and a safety property that depends on Chapter 5's probes. The chapter's densest block |\n223\t| §5 | medium | Small closed set of `kubectl rollout` verbs, plus one exact rule about what does and does not create a revision |\n224\t| §6 | medium | One distinction, drawn precisely, against a documented misconception — and a deliberate forward reference the reader must be told about |\n225\t| §7 | low | Three resources, each with one defining property |\n226\t| §8 | medium-high | An abstraction jump: resources that did not exist until someone declared them, and controllers you write |\n227\t| §9 | low | Synthesis |\n228\t\n229\t*\"If you only have 15 minutes\"* should point at **§1 plus the decision tree at the close of §7**, then Bearings #3. That is the highest exam-points-per-minute route through the chapter: the ownership chain is the structural key, and the decision tree is where traps #21, #22 and #23 all resolve."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"839b721c-4161-4462-926d-1dd8a865c1c5","uuid":"b28064db-4cca-43cf-8e88-605917221093","timestamp":"2026-08-24T13:06:37.193Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\.pipeline-state\\ch-06\\outline.md","content":"    - \"orphaning\"\n    - \"cascading-deletion\"\n    - \"replicas\"\n    - \"desired-replica-count\"\n    - \"manual-horizontal-scaling\"\n    - \"horizontal-scaling\"\n    - \"vertical-scaling\"\n    - \"horizontalpodautoscaler\"\n    - \"label-selector\"\n    - \"matchlabels\"\n    - \"matchexpressions\"\n    - \"selector-template-agreement\"\n    - \"overlapping-selectors\"\n    - \"deployment-strategy\"\n    - \"rolling-update\"\n    - \"recreate-strategy\"\n    - \"maxsurge\"\n    - \"maxunavailable\"\n    - \"minreadyseconds\"\n    - \"readiness-gated-rollout\"\n    - \"rollout\"\n    - \"revision\"\n    - \"rollout-history\"\n    - \"rollback\"\n    - \"revision-history-limit\"\n    - \"pause-rollout\"\n    - \"resume-rollout\"\n    - \"stuck-rollout\"\n    - \"statefulset\"\n    - \"stable-pod-identity\"\n    - \"pod-interchangeability\"\n    - \"daemonset\"\n    - \"node-local-facility\"\n    - \"job\"\n    - \"run-to-completion\"\n    - \"cronjob\"\n    - \"cronjob-schedule\"\n    - \"custom-resource\"\n    - \"customresourcedefinition\"\n    - \"custom-controller\"\n    - \"operator-pattern\"\n    - \"declarative-api\"\n    - \"dynamic-registration\"\n  commands:\n    - \"kubectl-get\"\n    - \"kubectl-describe\"\n    - \"kubectl-apply\"\n    - \"kubectl-scale\"\n    - \"kubectl-rollout-status\"\n    - \"kubectl-rollout-history\"\n    - \"kubectl-rollout-undo\"\n    - \"kubectl-rollout-pause\"\n    - \"kubectl-rollout-resume\"\n    - \"kubectl-delete\"\n\nfigures_planned:\n  - \"ch06-fig01-deployment-replicaset-pod-ownership\"\n  - \"ch06-fig02-rolling-update-maxsurge-maxunavailable\"\n  - \"ch06-fig03-recreate-vs-rolling\"\n  -