{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WnHLshDhVtKkYh3cNumnKV","type":"tool_result","content":"28\t- **Low:** Concrete, familiar concepts — study anytime\n29\t- **Medium:** New concepts requiring focus — study when alert\n30\t- **High:** Abstract or complex material — study at peak attention\n31\t\n32\t**Recommended split point:** after Taking Your Bearings #2. Sections 1–5 are the Deployment arc from start to finish; 6–9 are the rest of the family and what the pattern turns into.\n33\t\n34\t*If you only have 15 minutes: read §1 and the decision tree at the close of §7, then take Bearings #3. The ownership chain is the structural key to this chapter, and the decision tree is where three of the exam's documented confusions all resolve at once.*\n35\t\n36\t---\n37\t\n38\t> *\"A fleet is not a number of ships. It is an intention, expressed in ships.\"*\n39\t> — Lodestar Ledgers\n40\t\n41\t---\n42\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"839b721c-4161-4462-926d-1dd8a865c1c5","uuid":"dd6adf7d-afa7-44a0-9e4e-1ca418458111","timestamp":"2026-08-24T13:09:23.373Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\.pipeline-state\\ch-06\\draft-v1-prevoice.md","content":"- **Low:** Concrete, familiar concepts — study anytime\n- **Medium:** New concepts requiring focus — study when alert\n- **High:** Abstract or complex material — study at peak attention\n\n**Recommended split point:** after Taking Your Bearings #2. Sections 1–5 are the Deployment arc from start to finish; 6–9 are the rest of the family and what the pattern turns into.\n\n*If you only have 15 minutes: read §1 and the decision tree at the close of §7, then take Bearings #3. The ownership chain is the structural key to this chapter, and the decision tree is where three of the exam's documented confusions all resolve at once.*\n\n---\n\n> *\"A fleet is not a number of ships. It is an intention, expressed in ships.\"*\n> — Lodestar Ledgers\n\n